KEY ESTIMATION RESULTS — worldbank_education_gdp.csv
Outcome: ln(GNI per capita, constant 2015 US$).  Regressor: edu expend. share (% of GNI).
Semielasticity = % change in GNI pc per 1-pp change in edu share. HC1 robust SEs unless noted.

PART A  DESCRIPTIVES (contemporaneous)
  LMC (n=41, 1975-2015):  corr(edu,GNIpc) = -0.481; semielast = -0.447 (SE 0.242, p=0.065); R2=0.189
  SSA (n=5,  2011-2015):  corr = -0.966;          semielast = -0.100 (SE 0.008, p<0.001); R2=0.936

PART B  PRIMARY: pooled interaction, common 2011-2015 window (N=10, df_resid=6, R2=0.985)
  ln(GNIpc) = 9.598 - 0.659*edu - 1.886*SSA + 0.559*(edu x SSA)
  b1 (LMC slope)      = -0.659 (SE 0.086), p<0.001
  b3 (Edu x SSA)      = +0.559 (SE 0.087, HC1; 0.089 OLS; 0.071 HAC), t=6.44, p=0.0007
  b1+b3 (SSA slope)   = -0.100 (SE 0.008), p<0.001
  With linear time trend (df=5): b3 = +0.315 (SE 0.086), p=0.0002

PART C  GROUP-SPECIFIC
  LMC 1975-2015:  -0.447 (SE 0.242, p=0.065), R2=0.189, n=41
  LMC 2011-2015:  -0.659 (SE 0.086), n=5
  SSA 2011-2015:  -0.100 (SE 0.008), n=5
  LMC 1991-2015 with controls (n=25, R2=0.972): edu -0.245 (SE 0.127, p=0.054);
     secondary enroll +0.028 (p<0.001), labor force +0.059 (p=0.022), exports n.s.
  2011-2015 + secondary enroll: LMC edu -0.318 (p=0.077); SSA edu -0.133 (p<0.001)

PART D  LAGS (LMC full sample)
  edu(t-1): -0.413 (p=0.087); edu(t-2): -0.354 (p=0.152); edu(t-5): -0.066 (p=0.787); 5-yr avg: -0.803 (p<0.001)

PART E  FIRST-DIFFERENCE / AR(1)
  LMC d_ln ~ d_edu: +0.022 (SE 0.016, p=0.161), R2=0.036  -> association vanishes
  LMC d_ln ~ d_edu + edu(t-1): d_edu +0.002 (ns); edu_lag -0.032 (p=0.064)
  LMC ln_t ~ ln_{t-1} + edu(t-1) [AR(1)]: rho=1.036; edu -0.019 (SE 0.019, p=0.312) -> level assoc. is trend-driven
  SSA first-diff (n=4): -0.052 (SE 0.046, p=0.263)

INTERPRETATION
- Naive contemporaneous association is NEGATIVE in both groups (income levels are negatively
  correlated with the education-spend share of GNI) — consistent with reverse income scaling,
  not a causal growth effect.
- The comparison (common 2011-2015 window): SSA's semi-elasticity (-0.10) is materially SHALLOWER
  (less negative, ~15% of LMC's magnitude) than LMC's (-0.66); interaction b3 = +0.56, p~0.001.
- Once income persistence is controlled (FD/AR1), the level association essentially disappears
  for LMC; SSA has only 5 income years, so robust inference on SSA is not possible.
- Caveats: GNI not GDP; edu spend as % of GNI not % of govt. expenditure; 2 aggregate units; N=10.
